...

Each time, adding 2 legs per dog added. We need to reach 84 legs. From 0 dogs, legs are 58. Difference needed: 84-58=26. Each dog adds 2 legs, so 26/2=13 dogs. Thus, 13 dogs, 16 chickens.

This is another way to approach the problem using a tabular method, which is good for visual learners.

