For the equation approach, I can set up an equation where the total number of oranges is equal to the number of children multiplied by the number each gets plus the remainder. So, 26 = 5x + r, where x is the number of oranges per child and r is the remainder. Solving for x and r, since 5x must be less than 26, trying x=5 gives 25, so r=1. Again, same result.

